  v4_senescence_bench: "ADDED 2026-06-22 — S5 chose Option F (empirical-first) for H_rest senescence
               (docs/spec_revision/plan/theory-hrs-01/h_rest_senescence.vsm). H_rest (state[5]) is now a slow running entropy
               FLOOR (EMA rate H_REST_EMA=0.001, sampled ONLY when stasis_cos≥θ_stasis). state[12]
               (calibrated stasis_H) stays FIXED ⇒ h_rest_drift = state[5]−state[12] is the SENESCENCE
               signal, LOGGED in CSV/debug/plotter. OBSERVE-DON'T-IMPOSE verified: compute_L uses
               state[4], compute_stasis_cos uses the global stasis_H — neither reads state[5], so the
               CONTROL LAW IS UNCHANGED. The 8-step protocol (esp. step 8) now MEASURES whether H_rest
               drifts; then fit Law A (Landauer/soplo, leading hypothesis) to the observed drift.
               Why A over the composite D: falsifiable + identifiable + first-principles (Landauer per
               soplo) — the composite is the earned endpoint, not the start. +H_REST_EMA adds 0 SRAM
               (a #define); h_rest_drift adds ~0 (computed inline). C6 budget unaffected.",
  next_step:  "rmw3 opens EXP-NB-01.ino in Arduino IDE → Verify (confirms C6/compile) → builds circuit
               (Arduino Nano gen-1 + 2 photoresistors + white LED + 5-LED bar) → flash → run 8-step protocol.",
  blocked_on: "physical circuit + IDE compile [rmw3/S5]. Firmware side is DONE pending C6.",
